    "updated_at": "2026-07-09T13:49:02Z",
    "body": "Hmm probably the flat tree isn't quite right, because we want to look at delegatesFocus. (The fact of the matter is that we do expose the existence of delegatesFocus=true closed shadow roots currently)\n\nPerhaps we want to add something along the lines of\n> If *descendant* is a [shadow host](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#element-shadow-host) whose [shadow root](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element-shadow-root)'s [delegates focus](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#shadowroot-delegates-focus) is true, \n>> Let *autofocusDelegate* be the autofocus delegate for *descendant*'s shadow root.\n>> If *autofocusDelegate* is not null, return *autofocusDelegate*.\n>> Continue.\n\n> If *descendant* is a slot element, and *descendant*'s assigned nodes is not empty,\n>> For each node *node* of *descendant*'s assigned nodes,\n>>>  Let *autofocusDelegate* be the autofocus delegate for *node*.\n>>> If *autofocusDelegate* is not null, return *autofocusDelegate*.\n\n>> Continue.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
